col9_Please explain:
The forest possibilities defined by the Chief Forester correspond, for a given management unit or local forest, to the maximum volume of annual wood harvests by species or group of species that can be harvested while ensuring renewal and the evolution of the forest based on the applicable sustainable forest management objectives, including those aimed at:

- the sustainability of the forest environment;
- the impact of climate change on forests;
- the natural dynamics of forests, including their composition, age structure and spatial distribution;
- maintaining and improving the productive capacity of forests;
- diversified use of the forest environment.
